-- MUST BE FLAGGED: NUMBER_DRIFT
-- Invariant: a number written into a sentence must agree with the number beside it, because the two
-- will be changed at different times. A mode said "first to 50" while its scoreTarget said 100, a
-- few lines apart in the same table, because a change to the number never reached the sentence.
--
-- This fixture is also the string-content trap: a check on what a string SAYS is dead if it is fed
-- source with the string literals blanked out (tools/verify.py:31 does exactly that). If this stops
-- being flagged, check what the rule is being handed before you change the rule.

local NumberBad = {}

NumberBad.Modes = {
	FixtureDeathmatch = {
		scoreTarget = 100,
		roundSeconds = 600,
		description = "First to 50 eliminations takes it.",
	},
}

return NumberBad
